WEBVTT

NOTE
Kind: captions
Source: Articulate Closed Captions Editor
Source Version: 3.117.36909.0

00:00:00.842 --> 00:00:05.407
Devon stops at the door of Room 2. The brass plaque beside it says Survivors

00:00:05.557 --> 00:00:09.886
Support Group. Down the hall, a pride flag is pinned to the corkboard above

00:00:10.036 --> 00:00:15.010
the reception desk, and the washroom signs read All-Gender Washroom. Devon

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:18.770
read the centre’s mission statement three times before signing up. They

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:21.258
breathe out. They step in.

00:00:22.108 --> 00:00:25.015
Priya, the facilitator, smiles.

00:00:25.242 --> 00:00:27.334
You must be Devon. Welcome.<break time="0.75s"/>

00:00:28.142 --> 00:00:30.152
She nods toward the circle of folding chairs.<break time="0.75s"/>

00:00:31.142 --> 00:00:33.390
There’s tea before we start, if you want some.<break time="0.75s"/>

00:00:34.408 --> 00:00:38.897
Devin takes the seat closest to the door. Across the circle sits Margaret,

00:00:39.048 --> 00:00:42.385
knitting needles clicking. Margaret glances up.<break time="0.75s"/>ok

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:45.281
Hey. Is this your first time here?

00:00:45.675 --> 00:00:47.758
Devin nods.

00:00:47.975 --> 00:00:53.750
Priya opens the session. She reads the group agreements aloud: confidentiality,

00:00:53.901 --> 00:00:56.232
no advice unless asked,

00:00:56.408 --> 00:00:59.537
use the name and pronouns each person shares.

00:00:59.975 --> 00:01:04.868
Tonight we have Devon joining us. Devon, would you like to introduce yourself?

00:01:05.709 --> 00:01:09.070
I’m Devon. I use they/them pronouns.

00:01:09.175 --> 00:01:12.541
Devon’s voice is steady, but their hand stays in the pocket of their hoodie.

00:01:12.691 --> 00:01:16.300
<break time="0.75s"/>The check-in moves around the circle. When it reaches

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:19.177
Margaret, she leans forward and looks across at Devon.

00:01:19.975 --> 00:01:25.185
I just want to say, I’m so glad she came tonight. It’s hard, that first step.

00:01:25.336 --> 00:01:30.785
I remember when I came. She’ll feel at home here, I promise.<break time="0.8s"

00:01:31.742 --> 00:01:36.473
Priya opens her mouth. She glances at Devin. Devin’s eyes are on the carpet.

00:01:36.623 --> 00:01:40.549
Priya closes her mouth. She writes the word pronouns in her notebook and

00:01:40.699 --> 00:01:44.147
underlines it. The check-in continues.

00:01:45.042 --> 00:01:49.215
Twenty minutes in, Margaret is sharing her own story. She circles back.

00:01:50.042 --> 00:01:54.304
And it’s people like her, like Devon, who give me hope. 

00:01:54.696 --> 00:01:59.127
When she waked in tonight, I thought, "Look at her, so brave."

00:01:59.775 --> 00:02:04.344
Priya looks down at her notebook. She does not speak. Devin’s tea has gone

00:02:04.494 --> 00:02:06.503
cold. They have not touched it.

00:02:07.575 --> 00:02:10.433
The third time, Devon stands.

00:02:10.342 --> 00:02:13.703
Sorry. I just need to step out for a minute.

00:02:13.375 --> 00:02:14.965
Priya nods.

00:02:15.042 --> 00:02:18.149
Of course. Take your time.

00:02:18.342 --> 00:02:22.911
Devon walks past the all-gender washroom sign, past the pride flag at reception,

00:02:23.056 --> 00:02:25.939
out through the front doors into the parking lot.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.966
They do not come back.

00:02:28.109 --> 00:02:32.517
The session ends at nine. Priya helps stack the chairs. Margaret pats her

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:33.478
arm on the way out.

00:02:34.342 --> 00:02:37.356
Such a great group tonight. Thanks for facilitating.

00:02:37.942 --> 00:02:42.676
When the room is empty, Priya sits down in Devon’s chair. She opens her laptop.

00:02:42.826 --> 00:02:43.874
She types:

00:02:44.942 --> 00:02:50.547
Hi Devon, I wanted to check in after tonight. I noticed...

00:02:51.209 --> 00:02:55.214
The cursor blinks. She deletes the sentence. She tries again.

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:59.226
Hi Devon, I’m so sorry about...

00:03:00.109 --> 00:03:04.835
She deletes that too. She closes the laptop. She turns off the lights in

00:03:04.985 --> 00:03:06.917
Room 2 and locks the door.

00:03:07.676 --> 00:03:10.585
At next Wednesday's meeting, Devon's chair is empty.

00:03:10.735 --> 00:03:14.000
Margaret is knitting. The pride flag is still pinned

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:16.889
to the corkboard at reception.

